---
// Privacy policy. Rule from HouseRules.md: never promise more than the code does.
// Update it (and HouseRules) when analytics or ads are added (PLAN.md, stage 7).
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { MAX_PDF_BYTES } from "../lib/dryer";

const h2 = "card-title text-heading";
const p = "body";
const list = "body flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 pl-5";
const maxMb = MAX_PDF_BYTES / (1024 * 1024);
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy · Toolito"
  description="How Toolito handles your files: most tools run on your device, and the PDF compressor deletes your file right after each load."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="2026-10-23"
>
  <p class={p}>
    The short version is posted on the wall as our <a class="underline" href="/#house-rules">House rules</a>. This page says the same thing in more detail.
  </p>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <h2 class={h2}>1. Most machines never see your files</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Compress image, Convert image, Merge PDF and Split PDF run entirely in your browser. Your files are opened, processed and saved on your own device.
      They are never sent to us or to anyone else.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <h2 class={h2}>2. The dryer (Compress PDF) is the exception</h2>
    <p class={p}>Compressing a PDF needs our server, so that one tool works differently:</p>
    <ul class={list}>
      <li>Your PDF (up to {maxMb} MB) is sent over an encrypted connection (HTTPS) to our server, which runs on Google Cloud Run.</li>
      <li>It is compressed in a temporary folder and deleted as soon as the compressed file is sent back to you — also if something goes wrong.</li>
      <li>We never store your PDF, and we never record its name or its content.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <h2 class={h2}>3. What our hosting providers record</h2>
    <ul class={list}>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Cloud</strong> runs the server. Like most hosting, it keeps a request log for each call to the dryer: your IP address, the time, the
        address requested, the response size and status, and your browser's user agent. We use it only to keep the service working and safe. Google
        keeps these logs for about 30 days.
      </li>
      <li>To stop abuse, the server counts requests per IP address for one minute, in memory only. The count is not stored.</li>
      <li>The website itself is a set of static pages served by a hosting provider, which may keep similar technical logs.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <h2 class={h2}>4. No cookies, no tracking, no accounts</h2>
    <ul class={list}>
      <li>Toolito does not use cookies, does not ask you to sign up, and does not track you across sites.</li>
      <li>There are no ads and no analytics today. If that changes, this policy and the House rules will be updated first.</li>
      <li>Fonts and every other file are served from our own site, so no third party learns that you visited.</li>
      <li>To work offline, your browser stores a copy of the site (not your files). You can remove it by clearing this site's data in your browser.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <h2 class={h2}>5. Changes</h2>
    <p class={p}>If we change how Toolito handles data, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
